meta {
  name: rotate-table-qr
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/admin/v1/tables/{{admin_table_uid}}/qr/rotate
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{access_token}}
}

tests {
  test("responds 200 and returns a NEW url", function () {
    expect(res.status).to.equal(200)
    expect(res.body.data.qr_url).to.include("/t/")
  })
}

docs {
  # Rotate a table's QR token

**Destructive to a physical object.** The printed sticker on that table stops working immediately
and must be reprinted -- a diner scanning the old one gets a dead end.

This is the recovery path for a code that leaked: photographed and posted online, or on a card that
walked off. It is why the token is rotatable at all (docs/DECISIONS.md D4).

Careful with the seeded tables: rotating table 1 invalidates the `qr_token` in your environment, and
`public / scan-table` will start answering `TX_TBL_004` until you update it.
}
